.TH SUNSHINE-STREAM-UNDO 1 "2026-10-10" "sunshine-stream-undo" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sunshine-stream-undo \- restore the native display mode after a Sunshine stream
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sunshine-stream-undo
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sunshine-stream-undo
restores output
.B DP\-2
to the native 2560x1440@240 mode via
.BR kscreen-doctor (1),
then polls up to 30 seconds for the mode to apply.
Takes no arguments and reads no environment.
.SH EXAMPLES
Sunshine post-stream hook:
.IP
.EX
sunshine-stream-undo
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Native mode restored.
.TP
.B 1
Mode did not apply within 30 s, or output not found.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sunshine-stream-prep (1),
.BR sunshine-gamescope-run (1),
.BR kscreen-doctor (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written for local use.
